   "date": "2021-10-28",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Financial Accountability Regime Bill 2021 extends accountability obligations from banks to the insurance and superannuation sectors, requiring accountable entities to defer at least 40% of variable remuneration for four years and granting APRA and ASIC joint administration and enforcement powers, with commencement from 1 July 2022 for banks and 1 July 2023 for others."
  }
